{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02C3", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{categories-lemma-equivalence-categories}\n", "suffix": "\n\\end{lemma}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0a1d8a0e75d1d6982717fbdeefc134c93e1582e775123f2252b14f2c6f51086b", "source_text": "A functor is an equivalence of categories if and only if it is both fully faithful and essentially surjective.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d3b1a8bc56f43f345c6082539b8856da7bf1d77d6d49b82eaae5f19924d7567b", "unit_id": "tag:02C3:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02C3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{A} \\to \\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{B})$", "MATH_0004": "$j(X)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0006": "$i_X : X \\to F(j(X))$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:731074b42c00242c0e5fd5b9ef28eb782f8b1e08d25543b0ec86bdbd3e952762", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9d3c5c46114eec6e43ec84f524efe7f4b9ba1e513328c1615eb53338473ab1ea", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be essentially surjective and fully faithful. As by convention all categories are small and as <MATH_0002> is essentially surjective we can, using the axiom of choice, choose for every <MATH_0003> an object <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005> and an isomorphism <MATH_0006>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d182f6647f1fbad9bc5e9fc730d8d73fe8d585180d58780a7cd4e93b15bd66f8", "unit_id": "tag:02C3:proof001"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof_paragraph", "parent_tag": "02C3", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-construct-quasi-inverse}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{proof}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6247390cfab2169ec242d530b639df3a175e37efeb5d8cc6ec5f68ed55ae7def", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:19de4a24bc2659e085abcce3025cef579c91889a93264383916205179e07170e", "source_text": "Then we apply Lemma <REF_0001> using that <MATH_0001> is fully faithful.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:df864b3ea9f69b792315dbbf5e96b14c7fb65989881a92d8eec5ad3e602d189e", "unit_id": "tag:02C3:proof002"}
